Scenario-Based for AWS security

1. Someone exposed AWS keys on GitHub—what do you do?

Disable the keys immediately

Rotate credentials

Check CloudTrail for misuse

Enable GuardDuty

Educate team + prevent recurrence

2. How do you handle DDoS attacks?

AWS Shield

WAF

CloudFront

Auto Scaling

Rate limiting

3. How do you enforce compliance?

AWS Config rules

SCPs (Service Control Policies)

Security Hub standards (CIS, PCI)

Continuous audits

4. How do you isolate environments (Dev/Test/Prod)?

Separate AWS accounts

SCPs via AWS Organizations

Network isolation (VPCs)

Different IAM roles

5. How do you log and audit AWS activity?

CloudTrail (all regions)

Centralized logging account

Immutable S3 bucket

CloudWatch alarms on suspicious activity
